# NexusLink AI Workflow (IDE-side Rule)

> **Division of labor with MCP handshake instructions**
> - **InitializeInstructions** (UE handshake): capability routing table, meta-tool constraints, read/write naming.
> - **This Rule** (IDE-side): enforce discover tools → find paths → read/write; forbid guessing cap names/paths; fill project-level `PathFilter` prefixes.
>
> Source: `Plugins/NexusLink/Resources/AIRules.mdc` — diff generic sections into your project copy after plugin upgrades.

---

## 1. Four-step flow (required)

For UE assets / PIE / blueprints / Widget / material / behavior tree / GAS, **call MCP this turn first**, then answer. UnLua is [NexusLinkExt](https://github.com/bytepine/NexusLinkExt): discover those caps with `SearchCapabilities` when that plugin is loaded.

| Step | Tool | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 1 Discover capability | `SearchCapabilities` | Skip when cap name is known; otherwise `Query` with 1–2 **narrow** words (e.g. `blueprint variable`, `runtime actor`, `behavior tree`); **no** business feature names, asset names, or over-broad single tokens (see §2) |
| 2 Discover asset paths | `SearchAsset` | Requires `AssetType` + functional `PathFilter`; top-level `Assets`; typed search adds top-level `RecommendedGet`/`RecommendedManage` — prefer those in step 3 |
| 3 Read/write | `get_asset_*` / `manage_asset_*` / `list_runtime_*` etc. | `AssetPath` **only** from `assets[].path`; prefer `RecommendedGet`/`RecommendedManage`; when lists include `<k>_defaults`, missing fields equal that value (`{**defaults,**entry}`) |
| 4 Persist | `SaveAsset` or manage `bSaveToDisk=true` | Required after disk asset edits; BP/ABP/WBP may also pass `bCompile=true` |

**Meta-tools** `SearchCapabilities`, `CallCapability`, `SubmitFeedback` must use **MCP `tools/call` directly** — not `CallCapability(Capability="SearchCapabilities", …)`.

---

## 2. Prohibitions

- ❌ Invent a `GetAsset` aggregate tool (correct: `GetAsset*`, e.g. `GetAssetBlueprint`)
- ❌ Search `SearchCapabilities` with business terms (`ChestPVE`, `Dice`, `Attack`, etc.)
- ❌ Over-broad single-token `SearchCapabilities` queries: `blueprint` / `Asset` / `Runtime` / `Animation` (causes `SearchOverflow`; add action or subdomain, e.g. `blueprint variable`, `runtime actor`)
- ❌ Guess `/Game/...` paths; no `AssetType=all` + bare `/Game/` without filters
- ❌ Call `GetAsset*` without `SearchAsset` first (missing `AssetPath`)
- ❌ `GetRuntimeActor*` / `SetRuntimeActor*` without `ActorName` (call `ListRuntimeActors` first; wait for `bHasPlayWorld`)
- ❌ `ExecCommand` without a non-empty `Command`
- ❌ Call dangerous caps (`ExecCommand` / `ExecPython`, plus any `Dangerous` cap from [NexusLinkExt](https://github.com/bytepine/NexusLinkExt)) in Confirm mode without `Reason` (purpose, expected effect, why no safer dedicated cap)
- ❌ Retry after `ErrorKind=UserDenied` (user rejected this request)
- ❌ Call NexusLinkExt Lua caps without PIE / UnLua ready
- ❌ Guess `unreal.*` Python APIs — they differ per engine version; probe with `GetPythonApi` before `ExecPython`
- ❌ Assume `ExecPython` writes are undoable — plain `obj.foo = x` is not recorded; use `obj.set_editor_property(...)` (or explicit `obj.modify()`) and check the returned `bUndoRecorded`
- ❌ Ignore `FeedbackHint` — call `SubmitFeedback`
- ❌ Expect `success:true` on write success (check MCP `isError` and structured operation/section/compile/save errors; partial edits may remain; inspect `bRolledBack` / `UndoNote` before retrying a failed batch)
- ❌ Pass `assetPaths` / `actorNames` / `widgetNames` to capabilities (cross-target via `CallCapability.calls[]`)
- ❌ manage top-level `Fields`/`Rows`/`Keys`/`Widgets`/`ops` or bare `Action` synthesis (use `Operations[]`)
- ❌ Legacy keys: `blueprintPath`/`newPath`/`ownerWidget`/`FilePath`/`classPath` (see §3)

---

## 3. Parameter contract (Breaking)

| Canonical key / shape | Notes |
|---|---|
| Single target `AssetPath` / `ActorName` / `WidgetName` | One target per capability call |
| `CallCapability.calls[]` | Cross-target batch (SearchMode) |
| manage → `operations[{action,…}]` | Sole operation container |
| get → `PropertyPaths[]`; set_* → `updates[{PropertyPath,value,…}]` | read plural; write singular inside entries |
| `DestAssetPath` / `ScriptPath` / `OwnerClass` | replace `newPath` / `FilePath` / `ownerWidget` |
| spawn `AssetPath` + `ClassName` | replace `blueprintPath` / `classPath` |

Legacy keys → `ArgInvalid`.

---

## 4. Common intents → tool chains (examples)

| User intent | Flow |
|----------|------|
| Blueprint variables/graph | `SearchAsset(Blueprint, …)` → top-level `RecommendedGet` (usually `GetAssetBlueprint`) + `assets[].path`; if cap unknown, `SearchCapabilities(Query="blueprint variable")` |
| Create/edit blueprint interface | `CreateAssetBlueprint(ParentClass=Interface)` → `ManageAssetBlueprint` `AddFunction` / `AddInterface` |
| Behavior tree / decorators | `SearchAsset(BehaviorTree, …)` → top-level `RecommendedGet` (usually `GetAssetBehaviorTree`) |
| GA config | `SearchAsset(GameplayAbility, …)` → top-level `RecommendedGet` (skip if GAS not enabled locally) |
| Current editor map / open level | `GetEditorContext(Sections=["CurrentMap"])` — not `GetAssetLevel` (needs a known path) and not `ListRuntimeActors` |
| PIE actor properties | After `bHasPlayWorld`, `ListRuntimeActors` → `GetRuntimeActorProperty(ActorName=…, PropertyPaths=…)` |
| PIE blackboard / active node | `GetRuntimeActorBehaviorTree` (needs PIE + `ActorName`) |
| Console command | `ExecCommand(Command="…")` (`Command` required, non-empty; Confirm mode also needs `Reason`) |
| Screenshot | `CaptureViewport` for Game/PIE viewport or full window; `CaptureEditorPanel` for LevelEditor panel tabs and Actor `ViewAngle` shots (Editor only) |
| Editor automation via Python | `GetPythonApi(Target="unreal", Query="…")` to confirm the API exists on this engine → `ExecPython`; both need Python Editor Script Plugin, and `ExecPython` is disabled by default |
| Errors / crashes / PIE / packaged Game logs | Errors: `GetOutputLog(Preset="Diagnose")`. Logs from the next action: `GetOutputLog(Watch={categories,TextIncludes,TextExcludes,verbosity})` then `bCollectWatch=true` (side buffer; consecutive duplicates collapse to `Repeat`). `SetLogCaptureFilter` is the persistent category whitelist (Warning/Error always captured) |
| Unreal Insights trace | UE 4.26+ editor only. `ListTraces` → `GetTrace(Sections=["Summary","Frames"])` → pass a hitch frame's `StartTime`/`EndTime` into `Timers` and `Bookmarks`. UE4 Store entries have an empty `Path`; pass `TraceId` instead. Stopped `.utrace` only; `bAnalysisComplete=false` means call again. Not `GetOutputLog` |
| Game design docs | Project **knowledge-base MCP** if available — not NexusLink asset search |

